course: dictionary
lesson: 10468
title: Tuft: a small bunch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tuft is a small bunch of hair, feathers, grass or threads, growing or held close together at the bottom. You can work out the meaning from context: «a tuft of grass» tells you a tuft is a bunch of grass, and «two black ear tufts» on a lynx tells you they are bunches of hair.
explain: Look at what the tuft is on or in. «The black tuft on a lion's tail» shows it sits at the end of a tail. «Its tall ear tufts are only feathers, not ears» shows that a tuft can look like ears but is not.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «She searched for a tuft of grass to start a nest.» If you put "small bunch of grass" in place of tuft, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A tuft is a small bunch of hair, feathers, grass or threads.
fact: Tufts are growing or held close together at the bottom.
fact: Tufts of grass grow in sand dunes and fields.
fact: «The black tuft on a lion's tail» is unique among cats.
fact: Tufts are also the little bunches of thread on carpets or toothbrushes.
exercise: «A big bumblebee searched for an old mouse hole or a tuft of grass to start a nest.» What is a tuft here? | A tall tree | A kind of bee | A hole in the ground | *A small bunch of grass
exercise: «Its tall ear tufts are only feathers, not ears.» What are the ear tufts? | Bits of fur from a hare | *Small bunches of feathers | Little horns | Real ears that it uses to hear
exercise: Which of these is a tuft? | *A bunch of threads on a carpet | A deep, dark cave | A smooth, hard stone | A long, flat river
test: «The black tuft on a lion's tail is unique among cats.» What does tuft mean here? | A smooth, flat patch of skin | A thin, sharp claw | A loud noise | *A small bunch of hair
test: Tufts are also the little bunches of thread on carpets or toothbrushes. Where might you find a tuft? | Under the sea | In the sky | Inside a clock | *On a toothbrush
exam: Using the context of «two black ear tufts» on the Eurasian lynx, what is an ear tuft? | A black sock worn on the head | A tiny ear hidden under fur | *A small bunch of hair growing on the ears | Two black bunches of hair on the ears
